`WanPipeline._get_t5_prompt_embeds` tokenises with `padding="max_length",
max_length=max_sequence_length` (512) and runs the UMT5 encoder on all 512
positions, then throws most of them away: `u[:v]` keeps `seq_lens` rows and the
zero-pad puts the shape back.  The text encoder therefore costs what the BUDGET
is, not what the prompt is.

Measured on a tiny UMT5EncoderModel (4 layers, d_model 32, `videogen/run_t5.py
mode=6`, `videogen/mark_t5.py sq2`, grid: real tokens {8,32,128,480} x
max_sequence_length {64,128,256,512} x batch {1,2}, threads 1, repeat 2).
States: `ptok = batch*max_len`, `sq = batch*max_len^2/64`, `lsq = max_len^2/64`;
`rtok` = the summed REAL token lengths.

  out/videogen_t5_sq_base   (rtok declared, whole grid)
    t5_embeds = 18.8*rtok + 24,828.4*ptok + 20,690.9*sq + 3,773,576   69.3% irregular
    t5_enc    = -1.2*rtok + 24,402.1*ptok + 20,723.2*sq + 4,625,186   68.6% irregular

`rtok` gets a coefficient of -1.2 on the encoder call itself (18.8 on the
enclosing region, which also contains ftfy's per-character `prompt_clean`) --
the real prompt is free.  The two states
that carry the region are the padded token count and its square:

  out/videogen_t5_sq2_base_padded  (prompt shorter than the budget)
    t5_embeds = 25,688.3*ptok + 46,070.5*sq + 27,692*lsq + 6,565,689    18.3% irregular
      per-ptok   mkl_blas_def_sgemm_kernel_0_zen 10,497, mkl_vml_kernel_sTanh 7,232
      per-sq     mkl_blas_def_sgemm_pst 17,664, sgemm_kernel_0_zen 2,704
      per-lsq    index_select_out_cpu 4,608, mkl_vml_kernel_sLn 3,320

i.e. the projections and the FFN activation per padded token, the attention
matmuls per padded token PAIR, and -- UMT5-specific -- the relative-position
bias, which is rebuilt as one (1, heads, L, L) tensor in EVERY layer, hence the
unbatched `lsq` term.

The fix runs the encoder on the longest REAL length instead, rounded up to a
multiple of 8 with a floor of 16, and leaves the slice-and-zero-pad alone.  With
the attention mask, T5's masked scores are shifted by finfo.min and its position
bias is relative, so a real token's output does not depend on how many pad
positions follow it: in float64 the outputs at L = 16..512 agree with L = 8 to
1.55e-15, and in float32 every L >= 16 is bit-identical.

  out/videogen_t5_sq2_fix_padded
    t5_embeds = 693.5*ptok + 34.8*sq - 27.7*lsq + 6,694,193             66.1% irregular

Every padding coefficient collapses (ptok -97%, sq -99.9%, lsq to zero); the
residue is now the prompt's own quadratic, which this state set does not declare
-- with `rtok` declared instead (out/videogen_t5_sq_fix) the region reads
53.8*rtok + 422.1*ptok - 34*sq.  Instructions per encoder call, batch 1,
max_sequence_length 512: 8 real tokens 384.8M -> 8.07M (47.7x), 32 -> 8.46M
(45.5x), 128 -> 17.3M (22.2x), 480 -> 124.5M (3.1x).  Wall clock, same shapes,
1 thread: 112.7 -> 4.89 ms, 111.1 -> 4.25 ms, 112.3 -> 6.05 ms, 112.7 -> 82.9 ms.

At production (UMT5-XXL, 24 layers, d_model 4096, 512 vs ~30 tokens) the encoder
does 2,422 GMAC per prompt padded to 512 against 148 GMAC at 32 real tokens --
4.84 vs 0.30 TFLOP, 16.3x, and 21.8x against a 24-token prompt; each layer also
materialises a 33.6 MB score tensor and a 67.1 MB position bias where 0.13 and
0.26 MB would do.

What this does NOT fix: `prompt_embeds` is still zero-padded to 512, so the
transformer still cross-attends to 512 keys.  That padding is not removable
without changing the output -- `attn2` is called with `attention_mask=None`
(transformer_wan.py:569) and `to_k`/`to_v` carry a bias, so a zero prompt row
becomes a real key (measured: truncating 512 keys to the 32 real ones moves the
transformer output by 0.271 on a scale of 2.30).  `t5_repad` is unchanged at
81*ptok + 125,525, and `attn_qkv = 1,358*seq_len + 2,494.7*kv_len + 369,881`
(0.8% irregular, out/videogen_t5_kv) still bills 2,494.7 per padded prompt token
in every one of the ~3,000 cross-attentions per video.

Equivalence: `videogen/equiv_t5.py` over 10 encode points and 3 full pipeline
calls, 26 arrays / 11.6 MB -- prompt_embeds, negative_prompt_embeds, latents and
decoded video all BIT-IDENTICAL to pristine diffusers (`cmp_t5.py` worst
max|diff| = 0.000e+00).  With a floor of 8 instead of 16 the worst difference is
4.17e-06, from BLAS picking a small-matrix kernel below M=16.

--- a/src/diffusers/pipelines/wan/pipeline_wan.py
+++ b/src/diffusers/pipelines/wan/pipeline_wan.py
@@ -182,7 +182,20 @@
